# GD-24 (round 19, writer 10): settled; was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §2.4. L §2.4: "a key its index doesn't hold is refused, LOAD-KEY, §5.6" (L §8.3 `<key> is not a key of <index or kind>`).
# The old comment:
# L §2.4 sorts version items "then keys in index order"; x[b] names a key the list index ks doesn't hold (such a model
# doesn't load, LOAD-KEY, but its text is reprinted before load, E §3.1 step 1), which has no place in that order:
# REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED.
=== options reprint
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

index ks = [a]
input x[k in ks]: int

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  x[b] = 2
  x[a] = 1
=== expect
refused: LOAD-KEY b is not a key of ks (m.tally:14)
